er's NSE/BSE holdings \u2014 for on-shore ownership use B1 (named >1% holders) or C1 (N-PORT). These totals are NOT India ownership and must never be presented as such.","definitions":{"kind":"'adr' = depositary receipt over an Indian-listed company; 'etf' = US-listed India equity fund.","val_usd":"13F reported value in US dollars. \u26a0 The field was in THOUSANDS before 2023-01 and in whole dollars after; both are normalised to dollars here by report date, so multi-year comparisons are valid.","d_usd":"change vs the previous report date in the store \u2014 a VALUE change, so it mixes price and flow. Not a pure flow.","n_managers":"how many of the SCANNED managers reported that security."},"caveats":["The manager universe is a CURATED, BOUNDED sample matched by name against the real quarterly 13F index \u2014 not the ~6,000-filer universe (scanning all of it would be tens of GB). `coverage.managers_scanned` lists exactly who was included.","Securities are matched on ISSUER NAME and the CUSIPs are LEARNED from the filings (`coverage.cusips_learned`), not typed from memory. A newly-listed India ADR/ETF whose name does not match a pattern will be missed until a pattern is added.","13F is quarterly and lags ~45 days; it reports LONG positions only and nets nothing.","Put/call rows are option positions, kept and flagged but excluded from every ownership aggregate.","Several historic India ADRs have delisted (Tata Motors 2023, Vedanta 2021), so their series legitimately end rather than going to zero from a data gap.","\u2605 COVERAGE, NOT FLOW: the store is built forward and filers land over ~45 days, so a date with few filers shows a small total for that reason alone. Read `coverage.filers_by_date` before comparing two dates; `coverage.partial_dates` lists the thin ones, where a step in the value series is an artifact of who was read."]}}